## 725: Five Minute Durations as Fractions of an Hour

An hour is 60 minutes. Fraction equals duration_minutes/60:
45/60=3/4 (gcd15);
12/60=1/5 (gcd12);
15/60=1/4 (gcd15);
40/60=2/3 (gcd20);
135/60=9/4 (gcd15).
135 minutes exceeds one hour; its fraction is not capped at 1.
These are dimensionless fractions of the 60-minute reference, not hour counts
with an unconverted minute numerator.

## 726: Three Gram Masses as Fractions of a Kilogram

1kg=1000g. Ordered fractions:
125/1000=1/8;
260/1000=13/50 (divide20);
750/1000=3/4 (divide250).
Use mass divided by the same unit reference; do not use 100g.

## 737: All Twelve Fraction Reductions

1. 4/10÷2 ->2/5; 8/9 already relatively prime;
   6/9÷3 ->2/3; 9/12÷3 ->3/4.
2. 2/8÷2 ->1/4; 3/12÷3 ->1/4;
   10/2÷2 ->5/1 (integer5); 6/30÷6 ->1/5.
3. 15/60÷15 ->1/4; 88/11÷11 ->8/1 (integer8);
   2/100÷2 ->1/50; 50/100÷50 ->1/2.

Different source fractions reducing to1/4 are equal values, not distinct
elements of a mathematical set. Ordered source mapping still requires all
twelve locations; "already reduced"8/9 remains unaltered. Denominators nonzero.

